<title>USA: Jury finds no negligence in Reynolds tobacco case.</title>
<headline>Jury finds no negligence in Reynolds tobacco case.</headline>
<dateline>JACKSONVILLE, Fla. 1997-05-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>A jury found on Monday that R.J. Reynolds Tobacco Co. was not negligent in a closely watched wrongful death lawsuit against the tobacco giant.</p>
<p>After deliberating for eight hours over two days, the jury found that Reynolds, a unit of RJR Nabisco Holdings Corp., was not responsible for making an unreasonably dangerous and defective product.</p>
</text>
